{"title":"Overnight resilience: supervised restart, durable session-boundary resume, and a real-provider soak gate for `atl overnight`","objective":"Close the five stated gaps between the current bounded sequential runner and a resilient unattended overnight run — without weakening existing human gates: (1) an in-process watchdog that restarts a dead runner inside the already-confirmed budget, (2) durable per-session checkpoints so a restarted run continues only from durable boundaries and never replays an in-flight provider session (USAGE.md:136), (3) config-driven whole-night budget profiles instead of the hardcoded 120m/5-session defaults (runtime/atl-manager.mjs:417-418), (4) a machine-checked preflight for the documented 'AI session must remain open' host constraint, and (5) an opt-in soak test that exercises kill/restart/resume against a real provider, not just mocks.","constraints":[{"rule":"Restart is authorization-preserving, not a new launch: resume/watchdog may only re-drive sessions under a durable, previously confirmed run record; fresh unconfirmed launches stay impossible (atl-manager.mjs:398-400 requires --confirm; verification/overnight_host_test.mjs:8 asserts scheduled recovery stays confirmation-gated)."},{"rule":"Never replay an in-flight provider session; resume only from persisted session boundaries, and interrupted sessions stay excluded from recovery (USAGE.md:136; launch.mjs:453 run.json is the durable boundary)."},{"rule":"One global provider slot and shared time/session budgets are preserved (launch.mjs driveTaskUntilGate is the single spawn owner for run/overnight/queue, launch.mjs:158-161); existing caps stay: 1..1440 minutes, 1..20 sessions (atl-manager.mjs:419-424)."},{"rule":"The documented host constraint stands — an AI session must remain open; an open laptop alone is insufficient (USAGE.md:136). This plan preflights and documents it; it does not claim to remove it."},{"rule":"ATL still does not install scheduled tasks itself (USAGE.md:136): the watchdog is in-process and ATL-owned; OS scheduler integration remains generated, validated command plans (windowsScheduledTaskPlan, overnight_host_test.mjs:5-9)."},{"rule":"All state mutations stay inside state.mjs / launch / recovery domain modules; the watchdog consumes the same modules and never becomes a second state authority (constitution, .trust/specs/017-agentic-developer-control-plane/plan.md:100-111)."},{"rule":"Scope bounded to the five stated gaps: no daemonization frameworks, no multi-machine orchestration, no cloud runners, no new stages beyond supervisor + checkpoint + budget profile + preflight + soak."}],"risks":[{"risk":"Auto-restart becomes a crashloop that amplifies token spend (dead provider CLI retried all night).","containment":"Watchdog honors the shared deadline/session budget, uses bounded backoff with a max-restart cap, parks the run as watchdog-failed with a morning alert, and never spends after a detected capability failure (human-action blockers stay blocked per recovery.mjs:14)."},{"risk":"Resume replays partial work or corrupts the ledger.","containment":"Only session-boundary states (pending) are resumable; running/interrupted are never re-driven (USAGE.md:136); ledger schema is versioned via config/manager-state-contract.json with an idempotent, backup-first migration."},{"risk":"Real-provider soak test burns real tokens unattended.","containment":"Live mode is opt-in via an explicit flag/env gate, capped to a few short sessions in an isolated temp workspace, with a printed cost envelope before it starts; mock mode remains the CI default."},{"risk":"Longer whole-night budgets hit provider quota or subscription limits mid-run.","containment":"Budgets remain shared and enforced by driveTaskUntilGate; the run stops at the durable boundary and the ledger records the stop reason; usage telemetry keeps local budgets authoritative."},{"risk":"Host sleep/hibernate silently invalidates 'overnight' assumptions.","containment":"Preflight checks and clearly reports the open-AI-session / power constraints with a pointer to USAGE.md:136; dry-run refuses unattended start when preflight fails."},{"risk":"False green from mock-only tests.","containment":"Completion is gated on the live soak run once (manual gate), while mutation testing (atl_manager_lifecycle_model.py --mutation-test) guards the resume state machine against vacuous assertions."}],"completion_checks":[{"check":"Killing the runner mid-overnight-run and re-invoking resume continues only pending sessions; completed sessions are not re-run and the interrupted session stays excluded; run.json matches on-disk session logs afterward.","verified_by":"extended verification/overnight_recovery_test.mjs + python verification/atl_manager_lifecycle_model.py"},{"check":"Watchdog restarts a dead runner without a new interactive confirmation (durable record is the authorization), stops at deadline/session caps, and stops retrying after the crashloop cap with a recorded failure reason.","verified_by":"new verification/overnight_watchdog_test.mjs (mock runner that dies) + extended verification/overnight_host_test.mjs"},{"check":"Overnight budgets are config-driven with whole-night presets; out-of-range values are still rejected with the existing StateError; one-shot run defaults are unchanged.","verified_by":"new assertions in verification/overnight_host_test.mjs + verification/run_abort_test.mjs"},{"check":"Preflight runs on every overnight start and dry-run, and fails with an actionable message citing the host constraint when unmet.","verified_by":"extended verification/overnight_host_test.mjs"},{"check":"Live soak (opt-in, manual gate) completes a capped number of real provider sessions with a forced kill/restart, and the final ledger shows exactly the expected done/interrupted/done sequence with matching session logs.","verified_by":"new verification/overnight_soak_test.mjs --live (run once by a human; never claimed from mock runs)"},{"check":"No lifecycle regression: the state contract and mutation model still pass and no transitions bypass state.mjs.","verified_by":"python verification/atl_manager_lifecycle_model.py --mutation-test and atl validate in an isolated temp project"}],"acceptance_examples":[{"given":"An overnight run confirmed for 5 sessions where session 1 completed and session 2 was interrupted by a killed runner process","when":"The watchdog (or a scheduled `atl overnight recover --confirm`) restarts the run from the durable record","then":"Session 1 is not re-run, session 2 remains marked interrupted and excluded, sessions 3-5 proceed, and run.json ends with statuses done/interrupted/done/done/done matching the session logs under .trust/manager/overnight/<taskId>/"},{"given":"A provider CLI that is missing from PATH or fails on every spawn","when":"The watchdog hits its restart backoff/crashloop cap","then":"It parks the run with a watchdog-failure reason (no further spawns, no token spend), posts a morning alert, and the ledger records each restart attempt with timestamps"},{"given":"config/manager.json carries an overnight profile of ~480 minutes / 20 sessions and the operator runs `atl overnight --all --profile night --confirm`","when":"parseWorkerFlags resolves the budget","then":"The profile is accepted, caps of 1440 minutes / 20 sessions still bound it, `--max-minutes 2000` still throws the existing StateError, and the one-shot `atl run` default remains 60m/1 session"},{"given":"A laptop where no AI session is open or power settings will sleep the host","when":"`atl overnight --dry-run` (or a real start) runs the preflight","then":"It reports the specific unmet host requirement with a pointer to USAGE.md:136 and refuses to enter unattended mode instead of starting a run that will die"},{"given":"A real provider is configured and the operator explicitly opts into the live soak","when":"The soak harness runs capped real sessions and force-kills the runner after the first completed session, then restarts from the durable record","then":"The post-run ledger shows exactly done/interrupted(/done...) with byte-identical session-log counts, and the harness prints a pass/fail verdict with evidence paths — no claim of success is made until that verdict is observed"}],"selected_skills":["atl-implement (skills/atl-implement/SKILL.md — bounded self-correcting loops: one task, run its verifier, inspect the diff, repair only with new evidence)","atl-verify (evidence + Trust Verdict gate before any done claim)"],"proposed_worker":"rowan (builder per runtime/README.md:69-70; verification evidence handed to beacon at the verify gate)","implementation_steps":[{"step":1,"title":"Freeze the session-level resume contract (SDD gate)","detail":"Extend the overnight ledger schema in config/manager-state-contract.json and runtime/lib/launch.mjs (run.json writer, launch.mjs:453) with per-session status pending|running|done|interrupted|blocked, restart history, and watchdog events; migration is versioned, idempotent, backup-first.","tdd":"Write the failing contract/resume assertions first in verification/overnight_recovery_test.mjs before touching the writer.","files":["config/manager-state-contract.json","runtime/lib/launch.mjs","verification/overnight_recovery_test.mjs"]},{"step":2,"title":"Implement session-boundary resume","detail":"Add `atl overnight resume --confirm` (and queue-aware --all) that re-drives only pending sessions of a durable confirmed run; running/interrupted stay excluded per USAGE.md:136; all transitions via state.mjs/recovery.mjs.","tdd":"Failing tests first: killed-mid-run fixture in verification/overnight_recovery_test.mjs; lifecycle model must accept the new resume transitions.","files":["runtime/atl-manager.mjs","runtime/lib/launch.mjs","runtime/lib/recovery.mjs","verification/overnight_recovery_test.mjs","verification/atl_manager_lifecycle_model.py"]},{"step":3,"title":"Implement the in-process watchdog","detail":"New `atl overnight watch` supervisor: spawns/monitors the runner, restarts on death with bounded backoff and a crashloop cap, enforces the shared deadline/session budget, parks the run with a recorded failure, and emits a morning alert. OS scheduled tasks remain generated plans only (USAGE.md:136).","tdd":"New verification/overnight_watchdog_test.mjs with a mock runner that dies mid-run (no real provider in CI); extend overnight_host_test.mjs for the schedule/watchdog boundary.","files":["runtime/lib/overnight-watch.mjs (new)","runtime/atl-manager.mjs","verification/overnight_watchdog_test.mjs (new)","verification/overnight_host_test.mjs"]},{"step":4,"title":"Config-driven overnight budget profile","detail":"Move the hardcoded overnight defaults (120m/5, atl-manager.mjs:417-418) behind an overnight profile in config/manager.json; keep hard caps 1440m/20 sessions and one-shot defaults unchanged.","tdd":"Failing parseWorkerFlags assertions first in verification/overnight_host_test.mjs (profile accepted, out-of-range still rejected).","files":["config/manager.json","runtime/atl-manager.mjs","verification/overnight_host_test.mjs"]},{"step":5,"title":"Host preflight for unattended mode","detail":"Preflight on every overnight start/dry-run: verify an open AI session/host requirements and surface power/sleep risk with an actionable message citing USAGE.md:136; refuse unattended start when unmet.","tdd":"Failing preflight assertions in verification/overnight_host_test.mjs (fail-closed on unmet constraints).","files":["runtime/atl-manager.mjs","runtime/lib/launch.mjs","verification/overnight_host_test.mjs"]},{"step":6,"title":"Real-provider soak harness","detail":"New verification/overnight_soak_test.mjs: isolated temp workspace, capped short sessions, forced kill after the first completed session, restart from the durable record, ledger/log integrity assertions. Mock mode is CI-safe; --live is an explicit opt-in against the configured real provider with a printed cost envelope.","tdd":"Build the harness against mock mode first; the live run is the manual evidence gate, run once by a human.","files":["verification/overnight_soak_test.mjs (new)","runtime/README.md"]},{"step":7,"title":"Documentation, only after verifiers pass","detail":"Update the overnight/token-boundary section of USAGE.md (around line 136) and runtime/README.md: resume/watchdog/preflight contract, budget profiles, soak evidence instructions, and an honest statement of what is and is not solved (no OS-level scheduler install, host constraint stands).","tdd":"Docs diff reviewed against observed verifier output; no behavioral claims without a matching evidence path.","files":["USAGE.md","runtime/README.md"]}],"verifier_commands":["node verification/overnight_recovery_test.mjs","node verification/overnight_watchdog_test.mjs","node verification/overnight_host_test.mjs","node verification/overnight_soak_test.mjs","node verification/overnight_soak_test.mjs --live","node verification/run_abort_test.mjs","node verification/multi_queue_test.mjs","node verification/control_plane_task_run_test.mjs","python verification/atl_manager_lifecycle_model.py","python verification/atl_manager_lifecycle_model.py --mutation-test","atl validate"]}
